X:1
T:Yellow Bittern, The
T:An Bonn\'an Buidhe
N:Bunting's 1840 collection. "In Bunting's third collection (1840), p. 56, is
N:given a fine air, The Yellow Bittern: in 3/4 time...(,however, Forde's
N:tune) is in common time and is at least as good as that of Bunting: besides
N:being simpler and more vocal. Compare with 'Maire Aroon'" (Joyce). Sources
N:for notated versions: the index to Bunting's 1840 collection reveals he
N:noted the tune from a "blind man at Westport in 1802;" Forde noted the
N:melody from fiddler Hugh O'Beirne (Co. Limerick) [Joyce]. Joyce (Forde MS),
N:1909; No. 609, pg. 314. =D3 Canainn (Traditional Slow Airs of Ireland), 1995;
N:No. 104, pg. 88. O'Sullivan/Bunting, 1983; No. 77, pgs. 120-121.
